            "content": {
              "text": "<strong>Chapter 3 Overview</strong>"
            }
          },
          {
            "template_id": "paragraph_medium",
            "content": {
              "text": "In this first portion of this module, you have considered some of the paradoxes that define global energy development and studied basic trends in energy access, renewables and efficiency. You have also gained an understanding of how energy is a critical catalyst for development in all sectors, whether education, health, food or jobs. It powers the systems that enable these sectors to functions.<br /><br />However, energy trends manifest differently depending on local context. This chapter will focus on energy in UNDP’s five regional bureaus, focusing specifically on regional contexts, challenges, opportunities, and strategies to achieving SDG 7 (access to affordable, reliable, sustainable, and modern energy for all)."
            }
          }
        ]
